    {
      "block_id": "h3-54",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Policy Validator Integration",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "SearchReplace receipts in all statuses (`success`, `no_match`, `refused`) pass the content-light policy validator (``validate_receipt_payload`` and ``validate_event``). No forbidden fields or value-shape violations are produced.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-56",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Instantiation",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The abstract-class instantiation bug reported earlier was fixed in Phase 5 by restoring proper class indentation for ``_classify_status_from_error_kind``. SearchReplace now instantiates cleanly and exposes ``run()`` and ``build_receipt()`` as expected.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-58",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Remaining Risks",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **Legacy ToolError paths** (file not found, outside workdir, parse failure, content size, empty content, directory target, binary file) now return structured `SearchReplaceResult(status=\"refused\")` with domain-specific `error_kind`. Receipt emission follows automatically. Only truly exceptional filesystem errors (PermissionError, OSError) in `_read_file`/`_write_file` remain as ToolError — these are system-level faults, not tool outcomes. 2. **No end-to-end agent-loop integration test**. ``build_receipt`` + ``capture_tool_receipt`` pipeline tested in isolation; full ``_execute_tool()`` path not exercised. 3. **``warnings`` field** is currently safe (counts and tips only) but could theoretically contain contextual strings in future. 4. **``refusal_reason`` for ``count_mismatch``** passes through unsanitized because count-mismatch errors contain only counts and expectations — no file content. This is safe by construction but worth noting.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-60",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Existing Tests (in `tests/tools/test_hardened_tools.py`)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
